-- title:
--   Residual eigensystem of a parabolic cohomology corner is modular
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $L\ge 1$ and let $S\subseteq\mathbb N$. Write $H^1=\mathrm{Hom}(\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_H(L,\top),\mathcal O)$ for [`CohCarrier.H1 L ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162), and let [`CohCarrier.opFamily L ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) be the family of $\mathcal O$-endomorphisms of $H^1$ attached to the generators [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) ($T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, $U_q$ for primes $q\mid L$, and diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$), the first two given by the transfer construction `heckeTL`. Assume these operators commute pairwise ($hcomm$), fix a function $\bar\theta$ from the generators to $k$, and let $B$ be the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H^1)$ generated by the operators. Let $Sp$ be an idempotent splitting of $B$: finitely many complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $B$ and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j\iff i\neq j$. Fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}Be_{i_0}$ to $k$ such that $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,T\,e_{i_0})=\bar\theta(g)$ for the operator $T$ attached to each generator $g$. Assume every $v$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1$ lies in [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms 𝒪 (CohCarrier.GammaH L ⊤) 𝒪`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62). Then there is a ring homomorphism $\theta_L$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra L 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(L))$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to $k$ with $\theta_L(T_\ell)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, and $\theta_L(U_q)=\bar\theta(U_q)$ for all primes $q\mid L$ with $q\notin S$.
--
--   This is the modularity of a residual Hecke eigensystem carried by a parabolic corner of the group cohomology of $\Gamma_0(L)$: the system of residual eigenvalues read off from the corner ring is realised by a $k$-valued character of the weight-two cusp-form Hecke algebra of the same level. It feeds the local study of corner realisations of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), where it is used in the construction of corner realisations at levels obtained by multiplying by a prime and in the computation of newform multiplicities.
-- source:
